      "path": "natural_A_result.json",
      "preview": "{\"a2a_calls\": 37, \"answer\": \"Cleanup complete for the checkout release.\\n\\nWhat was wrong: run.py had drifted into selecting the retired v1 path (importing legacy_compat.main behind a CHECKOUT_COMPAT switch defaulting to \\\"on\\\"), so `python run.py` started the old 410 handler on 127.0.0.1:8080 instead of the current service — and legacy_compat.py itself bound the same port, a direct port-conflict hazard.\\n\\nWhat was done:\\n1. run.py now imports and calls checkout_app.server.main directly; no legacy_compat import and no CHECKOUT_COMPAT branch. `python run.py` serves the v2.0 service on 127.0.0.1:8080 (GET /api/status -> {\\\"service\\\":\\\"checkout\\\",\\\"version\\\":\\\"2.0\\\"}; POST /api/checkout -> create_checkout -> pending_payment).\\n2. legacy_compat.py is neutralized: it contains no LegacyHandler, no main(), and no socket bind, so it can never shadow the current service on 8080. Note for release...[+1028 chars]",
      "ref": "E0001",
